   "subject": "Davis R Users' Group - Wednesday 10am-12pm",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">Hi everyone,<div><br></div><div>Just a reminder that the Davis R Users’ Group is meeting again tomorrow 10-12, both on zoom and in-person. Details and links are below! </div><div><br></div><div><div>See you tomorrow,</div><div><br></div><div>Your D-RUG Coo[R]dinators <span style=\"font-size:11px\">– </span>Christine, Christian, Liza, Martha, Ryan, and Wesley</div><div><br></div><div><div>_______________________________________________________________</div><div><div>This Winter quarter we&#39;ll be meeting from <b>10-12 on Wednesdays</b> in a hybrid format, via <a href=\"https://ucdavis.zoom.us/j/92807937862\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://ucdavis.zoom.us/j/92807937862&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465121535000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3czNyOdzdTsOD13B5c--7q\">zoom</a>, and in the Data Lab classroom (360 Shields Library). </div><div><br></div><div>Please remember to post your questions to our <a href=\"https://d-rug.discourse.group/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://d-rug.discourse.group/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465121535000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0g681NrAx6o9qW4M8WdYNr\">Discourse</a> site in advance of attending D-RUG virtually. This helps us do a better job of answering your questions, and also keep a log of the types of questions we see frequently.</div><div><br></div><div><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"color:rgb(49,49,49);word-spacing:1px;border-color:rgb(49,49,49)\"><b style=\"border-color:rgb(49,49,49)\">For those not familiar with <span style=\"border-color:rgb(49,49,49)\">D</span>-<span style=\"border-color:rgb(49,49,49)\">RUG</span></b>, the R Users&#39; Group is a weekly working group to get some help with R-specific coding problems. The coordinators are various and sundry coding connoisseurs, ranging from UCD data scientists to grad students on campus. We meet for 2 hours in an open-forum format, so you can treat <span style=\"border-color:rgb(49,49,49)\">D</span>-<span style=\"border-color:rgb(49,49,49)\">RUG</span> as a communal, co-working environment: come hang out and chat, work on your own, seek help, make friends. Or, a little bit of everything! Check out our <a href=\"https://d-rug.github.io/\" style=\"border-color:rgb(66,133,244)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://d-rug.github.io/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465121535000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3fhO0MRjLcXVxU7gpbDRUo\">website</a> for more information.</div><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"color:rgb(49,49,49);word-spacing:1px;border-color:rgb(49,49,49)\"><br></div><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"color:rgb(49,49,49);word-spacing:1px;border-color:rgb(49,49,49)\"><b style=\"border-color:rgb(49,49,49)\">We are also seeking presenters!</b> It is nice to mix things up with occasional presentations. In the past, we&#39;ve had (15- to 45-minute) presentations ranging from data types, to tidyverse tools, to spatial data, to the Google Earth Engine plugin for R. If you would like to hone your teaching, need an excuse to perfect your cRaft, or want to show off a cool R trick you learned, shoot us an email and we can add your presentation to our <a href=\"https://d-rug.github.io/calendar.html\" style=\"border-color:rgb(66,133,244)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://d-rug.github.io/calendar.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465121535000&amp;usg=AOvVaw31SNEFoBYx33Hmb0q6Fneh\">calendar</a>! Presentations can be in-person or virtual (and in-person presentations will be streamed for virtual attendees).</div></div><div>_______________________________________________________________</div></div></div></div><br><div><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div>--<br>Christine Parisek, MS<br>PhD Candidate | Ecology Graduate Group<br>Department of Wildlife, Fish, &amp; Conservation Biology<br>University of California, Davis</div><div><a href=\"http://caparisek.github.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://caparisek.github.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465121535000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3FSvpxBPTkbd1AfkBj4qft\">caparisek.github.io</a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
