     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">Hi folks, <div><br></div><div>Special update! Tomorrow at 10am you will also have the opportunity to hear a short 20min presentation from one of your very own D-RUG Coordinators, Wesley Brooks. </div><div><br></div><div><b>Title</b>: Do e-bikes reduce car use? Design, simulation, and power analysis for a study of e-bike use in Sacramento<br><br><b>Abstract</b>: Micromobility services like subscription e-bikes and e-scooters offer people new modes of travel in urban environments. Meanwhile, minimizing car travel is important for limiting the negative effects of air pollution and CO2 emissions. Thus, micromobility services would be an environmental boon if people use them instead of driving - but it is currently unknown whether that substitution is happening. In this talk, Dr. Wesley Brooks will describe the design and analysis of a study that aims to measure the substitution of vehicle use with micromobility services. The statistical power of several candidate designs is simulated using a hierarchical Bayesian model based on integrating data from multiple sources and scales.</div><div><br></div><div>Happy coding,</div><div>Christine </div><div><br></div><div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
